{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>In the third month</b> Adjacent to what they said: a captive convert woman who is freed may not be married until three months have passed for her — just as Israel was freed and went out from the captivity of Egypt, He waited for them three months until the day of the giving of the Torah, on which they were betrothed to HaShem blessed be He:" "<b>לצאת</b> Three times in the Masorah: לצאת here. And the other: לצאת בני ישראל, concerning the matter of the house, and likewise here: בנו משכן (they built the Tabernacle). And the other: concerning the death of Aaron, in the fortieth year — לצאת בני ישראל — for the death of the righteous atones:" "<b>On this day they came to the wilderness of Sinai</b> On that very day of which it was said to Moses: תעבדון את האלהים על ההר הזה (you shall serve Elohim on this mountain)."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:36.093978943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}